Rules:
- Infer entityType from the file content and extension. For example: screens/forms → Form, menu definitions → Menu, batch submission defs → Submission, data layout defs → Data
- For properties: include any structured attributes you can identify (field names, column headers, action codes, status values, etc.)
- For crossReferences: identify any references to known artifacts (COBOL program names in CALL-like syntax, file names that look like data files, PL/SQL package calls via SQL, etc.)
- If the file contains only one entity (e.g. a single form definition), return one entity in the entities array
- Omit empty arrays
- Return ONLY the JSON object, no markdown fences, no explanation
